import gunbc.guarantee_rung { StructurallyGuaranteed }
import gunbc.rung_climb { AwaitsOneGrounding, GroundingDeclared }

data host_text_plus_is_not_judged_by_carrier_selection: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "host_text_plus_is_not_judged_by_carrier_selection" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead {
    found_at: FoundBelowTheLadder,
    standing: BelowCeiling {
      current: FoundBelowTheLadder,
      ceiling: StructurallyGuaranteed,
      blocker: AwaitsOneGrounding { grounding: GroundingDeclared { reference: DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.extdeps.languages.dag", decl_name: "dag_kernel_value_type_roster", field: WholeDeclaration } } },
      trigger_capability: "the seed can consume one kernel-spelling authority (dag_kernel_value_type_roster), either relocated under the name-to-path rule or reachable as a seed import -- sufficient for v1.compiler.infer_types operand_carrier_ref to ground every kernel spelling of one kernel value type (the bare String, v2.std.node String, std.host_text HostText) to one carrier, so a text operand pair is judged by v1.compiler.infer_types arithmetic_carrier_selection instead of being declined by operand_is_text."
    },
  },

  receipts: [
    "**host text + is not judged by carrier selection** (an arithmetic operator whose operand v1.compiler.infer_env text_representation_by_identity reads as text keeps the left-operand typing it had before carrier selection existed: v1.compiler.infer_types arithmetic_carrier_selection declines it through operand_is_text, and nothing judges the pair).",

    "INVALID STATE: an Accepted program in which `+` has a text operand and an operand of a different kernel value type or text representation -- host text beside a structural FreeMonoid<Char> String, or text beside an Int -- and is typed from its left operand with no carrier judgment.",

    "HARM: a mismatched operand pair reaches emission typed as the left operand; the wrong type surfaces at the first consumer that reads the result as its declared type, or not at all where both realize as one host string.",

    "WHY DECLINED, NOT JUDGED (gunbc#15610, 2026-11-01): the six '+' sites the v2 self-host emit refused (srv2 kh-q1e-diag2 at 35856d3e4346, gunbc 52191dc7…) were five host-text concatenations whose operands read 'Primitive(String) @ no carrier' against 'Primitive(String) @ v2.std.node.String' -- one kernel value type spelled two ways -- and one identity-erased operand. The authority that names both spellings as ONE kernel value type is v2.extdeps.languages.dag dag_kernel_value_type_roster, which lives in src/v2; seed imports resolve under dag/, so operand_carrier_ref cannot consult it and grounds only the spelling 'Int'. A dag/ copy of the roster would fork that authority (DESIGN section 3); comparing carriers by leaf name would admit a HostText-plus-FreeMonoid crossing silently (section 4); restoring left-operand fallback for carrier-less operands was ruled out. Declining text keeps those sites' typing exactly as on main and judges nothing new.",

    "SCOPE: numeric operands are unaffected. A carrier-less numeric pair still refuses ArithmeticWithoutCarrier (test.claim.arithmetic_carrier_witness w_nat_plus_unmodeled_carrier_refuses; test.claim.refinement_cast_wall_witness w_peano_nat_difference_is_not_the_refinement). The identity-erased operand (`state.count + 1`, typed 'Primitive()') is a separate reading, not this row: v1.compiler.infer_types operand_identity_unknown abstains on it as it does on a type variable, which is blind, not a judgment.",

    "RUNG: found BELOW the ladder -- the pair is accepted with no judgment, as it was before carrier selection.",

    "CEILING 3, structurally guaranteed: once every kernel spelling grounds through one authority, a text pair is judged like any other (same carrier: the operation's own; different representations: the declared text crossing or a refusal).",

    "REVIEW TELL: a carrier comparison by leaf name, a dag/ restatement of the kernel value type roster, or a text-specific typing branch beside the carrier selection.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
